# Cursor Cloud Extra High

Use MCP `cloud_launch`, `cloud_list`, `cloud_status`, and `cloud_result` (or `scripts/launch-cloud-extra-high.sh`). Set `GCS_CLOUD_REPO` or `CLOUD_REPO_URL` before create. `--name` REFUSE if a live `runStatus=RUNNING` Extra High already has that name (no twin remint). Leftover `ACTIVE`+`FINISHED` does not block. Directors must cloud_launch until ≥8 RUNNING per repo; count `runStatus`, not leftover `ACTIVE`. Check `scripts/cloud/running-count.sh`. Collect `cloud_result` includes bound `repos[0].url` (`repoUrl`) so you can tell Palemon vs grok-cloud-studio targeting. Palemon Linear is Living Sky (`LIV`), not Black Swan. Never Grok Bot as the grunt runtime. Do not print API keys. After `CLOUD_LAUNCH_OK`, a waiter A2A-pings the owning seat with result/context; do not block the Director turn on watch. Optional `GCS_WEBHOOK_SECRET` Cursor Cloud `statusChange` receiver can `FLEET_DONE` without `get_agent_run`. Never Bot CloudAgent.

`cloud_list` prints latest-run `runStatus` (`RUNNING` vs `FINISHED`), not only agent `ACTIVE`. ACTIVE+FINISHED leftovers are not live workers.
